NCCL in MANA's lower half (prototype)
=====================================

NCCL and its network libraries go into the lower half, like MPI: they are not
checkpointed, and a restart loads them again, so the job may restart on
another node or network.  The lower half's NCCL uses the application's CUDA
through the forwarding shims (../cuda-forward): there is one CUDA driver in
the process, the upper half's, which the DMTCP CUDA plugin checkpoints.  Use
it with --cuda (mana_launch --cuda, mana_restart --cuda).

The checkpointing of communicators comes from the nccl-mana-ckpt prototype
(virtual communicators, sequence consensus, point-to-point drain, teardown
before the GPU checkpoint, rebuild with a fresh ncclUniqueId).

Files
-----
  nccl_wrappers.c     The application's nccl* functions that take or make a
                      communicator (from nccl-mana-ckpt): virtual handles,
                      the sequence gate, the byte counts of the drain.
  nccl_forward.c      Generated: the other functions of nccl.h, forwarded.
  nccl_lh_thunks.cpp  Generated: mana_lh_ncclX() calls the lower half's ncclX
                      with the lower half's FS; it waits while the lower half
                      is closed for a checkpoint, except for MANA's own calls.
  nccl_lh.{h,cpp}     The glue of the thunks (lh_info->lh_nccl_dlsym).
  nccl_ckpt.{h,c}     The checkpoint phases (from nccl-mana-ckpt's plugin),
                      called by MANA's event hook (../mpi_plugin.cpp).
  nccl_cuda.{h,c}     The application's CUDA runtime, for nccl_ckpt.c.
  vcomm.*, inflight.*, dmtcp_kvdb_c.*   From nccl-mana-ckpt, unchanged.
  gen-nccl-wrappers.py  Generates the thunks, the forwarders and the stub.

  nccl_lh_audit.c     The lower half's audit module (libmana_lh_audit.so):
                      redirects a static CUDA runtime in libnccl (below).

  The upper half loads libmana_ncclstub.so in place of libnccl (the audit
  module, ../mpi-wrappers/mpi_stub_audit.c): libmana.so defines the
  functions.  The lower half loads MANA_NCCL_LIBRARY (default libnccl.so.2)
  on the first NCCL call (lower-half/lower-half.cpp, lh_nccl_dlsym()), with
  RTLD_DEEPBIND: the MPI library may link with another libnccl.

NVIDIA's binary libnccl
-----------------------
  It has a CUDA runtime linked in statically, whose integrity check fails
  against the lower half's libcuda, the forwarding shim
  (cudaErrorSoftwareValidityNotEstablished at ncclCommInitRank).  The lower
  half therefore runs with an audit module (LD_AUDIT=MANA_LH_AUDIT, set by
  mana_launch/mana_restart --cuda and only for the lower half's exec): once
  libnccl is mapped, before its relocation and constructors, every function
  of the embedded runtime (the local cuda* and __cuda* functions of its
  .symtab) that the libcudart.so shim also exports jumps to the shim's.  So
  libnccl uses the application's runtime, like a libnccl linked with
  libcudart.so, and its constructors' kernel registrations reach the shim,
  which replays them into the application's runtime.  This needs the
  library's .symtab (NVIDIA's libnccl has it).  A libnccl linked with
  libcudart.so (CUDARTLIB=cudart) is left alone.

Checkpoint and restart (../mpi_plugin.cpp)
------------------------------------------
  PRESUSPEND   One cut of MPI and NCCL collectives: mana_nccl_ckpt_begin(),
               then MANA's MPI drain, each round of which is also a round
               of the NCCL consensus (mana_nccl_consensus_round(); see
               ../seq_num.h).  A thread waits at the NCCL gate or the MPI
               gate only if both its NCCL and MPI communicators are at their
               targets.  mana_nccl_ckpt_quiesce(); the lower half closes;
               mana_nccl_ckpt_teardown(): drain NCCL point-to-point
               messages, destroy every communicator.  Then the CUDA plugin
               checkpoints the GPU.
  RESUME/RESTART  reset the sequence numbers; at restart, forget the
               lower half's NCCL functions and the real handles.
  RUNNING_AFTER  after the CUDA plugin restored the GPU and, at restart,
               after the new lower half's MPI_Init and MPI replay:
               mana_nccl_rebuild() creates every communicator again; then
               the application's threads may enter the lower half.

  Threads that NCCL creates in the lower half (proxy threads) call CUDA with
  the TLS of an upper-half "donor" thread (../cuda-forward/fwd-runtime.c,
  take_donor(); ../uh_wrappers.cpp, mana_fwd_provide_donors()).

Requirements and limits
-----------------------
  * A libnccl with a static CUDA runtime and no .symtab (stripped) cannot
    be redirected, and fails as above.
  * One GPU per process, and one application thread in NCCL or MPI at a
    time: the lower half's TLS is shared by the threads that enter it.
  * Tested on one GPU: each rank has a communicator of its own, so NCCL
    traffic between ranks, its point-to-point drain, and several nodes are
    not tested yet.
  * The communicators are destroyed and created again at every checkpoint,
    resume included (the CUDA checkpoint cannot take NCCL's CUDA IPC).
  * From nccl-mana-ckpt: communicator creation in progress during a
    checkpoint, ncclCommShrink/Grow, windows, registered buffers and custom
    reduction ops across a checkpoint are not supported; the p2p drain
    counts bytes, not messages.
